# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the contributor's platform does
# with the rest of the tree. A CRLF docker-entrypoint.sh does not fail visibly:
# the kernel reads "/bin/sh\r" as the interpreter and the container dies with
# "no such file or directory", naming a file that is plainly there.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux tooling, not by an editor on Windows.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
